From 30123801a279479f1dc9406d417e7bfa17b9f023 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:01:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Compose A's verified chain authority (df8fbafae) into the
 hosted-service roles, the runner and their readers

This brings only the modules the directory-replica and policy-mirror roles, the host-services runner (gate and
carriers) and their server readers need from worker A's immutable df8fbafae. They were composed from git objects
(rpc-priority/repo, A's base 9fdc1418c); A's tree was not edited.

Taken as A's blobs: A's base blob for each equals 4106c311's, so this IS the 3-way result.
  network/verified-chain.mjs  e55f0359eb26
  network/lease-reader.mjs  d77dbf772ca3
  network/directory-server.mjs  c48d1908606b
  network/host-policy-runtime.mjs  95930152ebc1
  network/service-index.mjs  d7350364a480
  test/verified-chain.test.mjs  774a4273d05d
  test/verified-chain-lifecycle.test.mjs  f1d0b20d7876
  test/lease-reader-verifier.test.mjs  eec9cf3c1949
  test/lease-reader-verifier-deadline.test.mjs  4c92a00b80b6
  test/lease-reader-terminal-snapshot.test.mjs  9c971b67b952

Three-way merged (git merge-file, ours / base 9fdc1418c / theirs df8fbafae):
- network/platform-host-policy-config.mjs, network/policy-carriers.mjs, network/host-services/roles.mjs and
  network/host-services/policy-mirror.mjs (on bb86e0ce's race fix): clean.
- network/host-services/runner.mjs policyCarrierFetch: 2 conflict hunks, resolved by
  host-service-rpc-closure/resolve-runner.py. C's injected snapshot (its gate's own authority) wins; otherwise A's
  configured chainAuthority applies. The RPC-quorum requirement applies only in legacy mode.

Effect:
- A role, or the runner's policy gate and carriers, given chainAuthority 'verifier' plus a LOOPBACK chainVerifier
  reads the local proof-backed verifier (unsafe tier, one pinned block, whole-operation deadline). It builds no
  provider client and has no provider fallback.
- Without that choice the legacy quorum is unchanged: 2 to 8 distinct providers, majority agreement.

Not composed (A's other consumers):
- cold-bootstrap, provider-settlement, usdc-bandwidth, management, native, windows, relays, lease-gas,
  host-admission and challenge-replica wiring;
- A's lease-reader-verifier "settlement pinned reads" case depends on usdc-bandwidth and is excluded by name in this
  tree's runs.
